If you like pretzel sticks, you are?

1079
00:39:35.260 --> 00:39:35.920
Oh, no.

1080
00:39:36.020 --> 00:39:37.320
There's one more I missed.

1081
00:39:38.280 --> 00:39:38.720
Rods.

1082
00:39:39.140 --> 00:39:40.340
Anybody like a rod?

1083
00:39:40.500 --> 00:39:41.120
That's what she said.

1084
00:39:41.400 --> 00:39:41.720
Oh, the big, long one.

1085
00:39:41.720 --> 00:39:43.100
What's the difference between a rod and a stick?

1086
00:39:43.100 --> 00:39:44.640
I think the sticks are tiny.

1087
00:39:44.860 --> 00:39:47.140
And skinny, and the rods are long and thicker.

1088
00:39:47.360 --> 00:39:47.860
Oh, okay.

1089
00:39:48.240 --> 00:39:49.000
No to both.

1090
00:39:49.300 --> 00:39:49.920
No to both.

1091
00:39:50.080 --> 00:39:51.340
So many TWSSs.

1092
00:39:51.600 --> 00:39:51.920
Okay.

1093
00:39:52.040 --> 00:39:56.080
Well, anyway, if you like a pretzel stick, you are laid back, yet confident, and prefer

1094
00:39:56.080 --> 00:39:57.100
to be by yourself.

1095
00:39:57.640 --> 00:39:58.580
You might be a stick.

1096
00:39:58.580 --> 00:40:00.380
I need to start eating some pretzel sticks.

1097
00:40:00.960 --> 00:40:04.920
If you're a pretzel rod person, you are laid back and outdoorsy.

1098
00:40:05.020 --> 00:40:07.020
A party is not your idea of a good time.

1099
00:40:07.180 --> 00:40:10.480
Instead, you would prefer to go camping or hiking with some good friends.

1100
00:40:11.380 --> 00:40:14.600
Finally, if you love a pretzel ring, you are health-conscious, upbeat.

1101
00:40:15.040 --> 00:40:18.740
You're a happy person, but you're concerned with your appearance.

1102
00:40:21.160 --> 00:40:22.680
And finally, rings.

1103
00:40:22.980 --> 00:40:26.120
If you're a pretzel ring person, you are health-conscious, upbeat.

1104
00:40:26.600 --> 00:40:29.560
You're a happy person, concerned with their appearance.

1105
00:40:30.380 --> 00:40:30.700
What?

1106
00:40:30.920 --> 00:40:31.700
I don't know.

1107
00:40:31.780 --> 00:40:34.380
Those two things don't seem to go together for me.

1108
00:40:34.960 --> 00:40:37.820
If I'm concerned about my appearance, I'm stressed.

1109
00:40:38.240 --> 00:40:38.840
All right.

1110
00:40:39.080 --> 00:40:40.120
I saw a theme.

1111
00:40:40.260 --> 00:40:42.160
And what does your pretzel say about you?

1112
00:40:42.460 --> 00:40:43.300
What is it?

1113
00:40:43.540 --> 00:40:45.120
Most of us are laid back.

1114
00:40:47.020 --> 00:40:47.500
Sorry.

1115
00:40:48.180 --> 00:40:50.060
I know, I know.

1116
00:40:50.180 --> 00:40:51.280
We are laid back.

1117
00:40:51.440 --> 00:40:54.180
If you like a pretzel, period, you're laid back.

1118
00:40:54.500 --> 00:40:54.900
You're laid back.

1119
00:40:55.400 --> 00:40:56.340
You're right.

1120
00:40:57.060 --> 00:41:00.840
The only person who's not laid back is a twist or a ring.

1121
00:41:01.080 --> 00:41:01.360
Yeah.

1122
00:41:02.160 --> 00:41:02.540
Mm-hmm.

1123
00:41:03.320 --> 00:41:04.040
All right, everyone.

1124
00:41:04.200 --> 00:41:04.940
Back to Stanley.

1125
00:41:05.160 --> 00:41:08.720
Another very memorable thing about Stanley is his basketball dribble.

1126
00:41:08.720 --> 00:41:11.600
Oh, his basketball skills, man.

1127
00:41:11.960 --> 00:41:12.360
Mm-hmm.

1128
00:41:12.620 --> 00:41:16.600
I went back to the shooting draft, and I found the description of that moment.

1129
00:41:17.280 --> 00:41:20.080
This is right at the start of the game, right?

1130
00:41:20.220 --> 00:41:24.820
When Michael grabs the ball after Pam throws it in, and the script says, quote,

1131
00:41:24.820 --> 00:41:27.960
quote, Michael fires the ball off to Stanley.

1132
00:41:28.300 --> 00:41:31.500
Stanley takes off clumsily downfield.

1133
00:41:31.900 --> 00:41:35.660
Michael is surprised at how bad he is, end quote.

1134
00:41:36.000 --> 00:41:42.200
I found it very amusing that it says he goes down a field instead of down the court.

1135
00:41:42.780 --> 00:41:44.360
Like, who wrote this?

1136
00:41:44.560 --> 00:41:46.380
Who wrote that description?

1137
00:41:48.100 --> 00:41:52.580
But that was all Leslie had to go off of, clumsily.

1138
00:41:52.820 --> 00:41:53.260
Yes.

1139
00:41:53.260 --> 00:41:59.700
And then he came up with this whole physicality of how Stanley dribbles, and it is hilarious.

1140
00:42:00.100 --> 00:42:07.740
Phyllis and I were reminiscing about this because, and you know, you, me, and Phyllis were all

1141
00:42:07.740 --> 00:42:10.720
seated together in the background of the basketball episode.

1142
00:42:10.920 --> 00:42:13.380
Yes, we were on that bench with a front row seat.

1143
00:42:13.560 --> 00:42:19.540
And Phyllis was like, that is still so funny to her.

1144
00:42:19.540 --> 00:42:24.820
She said that is her first memory of realizing the brilliance of Leslie David Baker.

1145
00:42:25.080 --> 00:42:26.360
And I remember that, too.

1146
00:42:26.480 --> 00:42:29.580
I remember we all were just like, what?

1147
00:42:29.780 --> 00:42:30.500
What is happening?

1148
00:42:30.780 --> 00:42:31.420
That is amazing.

1149
00:42:31.680 --> 00:42:34.020
So Leslie gets this question all the time.

1150
00:42:34.020 --> 00:42:36.940
He's always asked, how did you come up with that?

1151
00:42:37.140 --> 00:42:39.720
People want to know, is that how he really dribbles?

1152
00:42:39.720 --> 00:42:41.180
And the answer is no.

1153
00:42:41.640 --> 00:42:47.840
Leslie shared that that style of dribbling is modeled after someone he went to high school with.

1154
00:42:47.960 --> 00:42:48.300
Oh.

1155
00:42:48.540 --> 00:42:49.840
But that's all he'll say.

1156
00:42:50.020 --> 00:42:51.280
He can't name names.

1157
00:42:51.360 --> 00:42:51.620
No.

1158
00:42:51.860 --> 00:42:53.120
Oh, that's so good.

1159
00:42:53.360 --> 00:42:55.800
I wonder if that person, though, knows.

1160
00:42:55.800 --> 00:43:00.640
They know they went to high school with Leslie, and they've probably seen the office.

1161
00:43:00.860 --> 00:43:01.920
Do they know?

1162
00:43:02.420 --> 00:43:03.060
I don't know.

1163
00:43:03.680 --> 00:43:04.720
Yeah, I don't know.

1164
00:43:04.820 --> 00:43:07.540
I mean, if you dribble like that, it's pretty distinct.

1165
00:43:07.840 --> 00:43:08.280
I know.

1166
00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:12.360
We also got this question about Leslie's background work.

1167
00:43:12.580 --> 00:43:15.500
Fan question from Jane in Woodstock, Georgia.

1168
00:43:16.200 --> 00:43:21.840
She said, in talking heads that had the window facing the bullpen, I noticed that sometimes

1169
00:43:21.840 --> 00:43:27.320
Stanley's head was completely still, and sometimes you would see his head moving slightly as if

1170
00:43:27.320 --> 00:43:28.760
he was actually doing work.

1171
00:43:29.100 --> 00:43:34.400
Did Leslie have to be in the background for every single talking head, or was there a green

1172
00:43:34.400 --> 00:43:36.880
screen for times Leslie couldn't make it to set?

1173
00:43:37.400 --> 00:43:38.360
Emily R.

1174
00:43:38.620 --> 00:43:43.700
wrote in from Calgary to also say, did Leslie make overtime or bonuses for being

1175
00:43:43.700 --> 00:43:46.440
in the background of talking heads all the time?

1176
00:43:47.120 --> 00:43:52.500
Well, you guys, no, he did not make overtime for that or get a bonus.

1177
00:43:52.500 --> 00:43:57.840
He was amazing and steadfast and such a trooper for years and years.

1178
00:43:58.080 --> 00:43:59.660
There was no green screen.

1179
00:43:59.860 --> 00:44:01.320
That was always him.

1180
00:44:02.000 --> 00:44:02.600
Always.

1181
00:44:03.140 --> 00:44:03.440
Always.

1182
00:44:03.920 --> 00:44:05.300
And here's the thing, everyone.

1183
00:44:05.660 --> 00:44:12.260
We would do our talking heads in a clump either first thing in the morning or at the very

1184
00:44:12.260 --> 00:44:17.280
end of the day, and then the sort of middle of the day was our group work.

1185
00:44:18.020 --> 00:44:22.520
But if you weren't in the talking heads, you got to come in late or you got to leave early

1186
00:44:22.520 --> 00:44:23.720
after the group work.

1187
00:44:24.380 --> 00:44:25.500
But not Leslie.

1188
00:44:25.840 --> 00:44:25.980
No.

1189
00:44:26.780 --> 00:44:31.400
There were times when Leslie came in at five in the morning and he just sat in the background

1190
00:44:31.400 --> 00:44:32.780
for two hours.

1191
00:44:32.780 --> 00:44:39.200
Or he had to stay later at the end of the day to wrap out the talking heads.

1192
00:44:39.200 --> 00:44:41.840
And he never complained about it.

1193
00:44:42.040 --> 00:44:42.200
No.

1194
00:44:42.460 --> 00:44:50.160
And I think about that when they were deciding where we would all sit, we had no idea what

1195
00:44:50.160 --> 00:44:52.120
shots we would be in the background of.

1196
00:44:53.160 --> 00:44:56.720
I really lucked out because I was behind that big partition.

1197
00:44:57.140 --> 00:44:57.460
Yeah.

1198
00:44:57.880 --> 00:45:00.760
So I was often not seen.

1199
00:45:00.900 --> 00:45:03.920
That's why I would have to walk out to the copier so many times.

1200
00:45:04.080 --> 00:45:04.220
Yeah.

1201
00:45:04.860 --> 00:45:07.380
But Leslie was right in the middle of the bullpen.

1202
00:45:07.380 --> 00:45:12.120
But what he didn't realize is he was right behind that chair where they would end up having

1203
00:45:12.120 --> 00:45:13.140
the conference room scenes.

1204
00:45:13.220 --> 00:45:14.400
And no one could have known that.

1205
00:45:14.580 --> 00:45:14.780
No.

1206
00:45:14.880 --> 00:45:16.860
That was sort of found as the show went.

1207
00:45:17.080 --> 00:45:21.320
And most of the time they could frame out Phyllis or they could frame out Creed who sort

1208
00:45:21.320 --> 00:45:22.760
of sits in that same corridor.

1209
00:45:23.320 --> 00:45:23.680
Mm-hmm.

1210
00:45:24.000 --> 00:45:26.440
But they couldn't frame out Stanley.

1211
00:45:26.900 --> 00:45:27.280
No.

1212
00:45:27.440 --> 00:45:28.860
His desk is right there.

1213
00:45:29.020 --> 00:45:29.880
Right there.

1214
00:45:30.680 --> 00:45:35.540
Next, we have a fan question from Sarah B., who is originally from Sweden but lives in

1215
00:45:35.540 --> 00:45:36.240
Salt Lake City.

1216
00:45:36.760 --> 00:45:39.780
Sarah said, Leslie did a fabulous job as Stanley.

1217
00:45:39.960 --> 00:45:44.700
And as the most viewed background actor, I'm assuming he must have gotten quite bored.

1218
00:45:45.020 --> 00:45:49.040
What did he do to entertain himself during all those shots?

1219
00:45:50.460 --> 00:45:54.400
Well, Sarah, Leslie said he did a lot of online shopping.

1220
00:45:55.200 --> 00:45:58.720
Once he even helped Phyllis shop for her Emmy dress.

1221
00:45:58.720 --> 00:45:59.380
Yes, yes.

1222
00:46:00.260 --> 00:46:03.820
I remember him saying how thankful he was when we got internet.

1223
00:46:04.660 --> 00:46:06.340
That was a game changer for him.

1224
00:46:06.440 --> 00:46:08.940
But he would often look things up for us.

1225
00:46:09.120 --> 00:46:14.060
If you said, just even in passing, like, oh, I need to get new bedding and I've been trying

1226
00:46:14.060 --> 00:46:17.180
to look for like, you know, a blue comforter.

1227
00:46:17.520 --> 00:46:18.900
He would look up things for you.

1228
00:46:19.040 --> 00:46:23.000
I remember the year that Phyllis wanted to get Christmas stockings.

1229
00:46:23.000 --> 00:46:27.460
And he searched so many Christmas stockings for her.

1230
00:46:27.800 --> 00:46:30.180
She had a very specific thing she wanted.

1231
00:46:30.200 --> 00:46:32.080
I remember it being a whole conversation.

1232
00:46:32.420 --> 00:46:35.680
Well, you know, we also got another fan mail flurry.

1233
00:46:35.860 --> 00:46:40.720
And it's about the relationship between the characters of Stanley and Phyllis.

1234
00:46:41.120 --> 00:46:43.820
There are so many fan theories about them.

1235
00:46:44.620 --> 00:46:50.680
There are articles, YouTube compilations, Reddit threads all about Phyllis and Stanley.

1236
00:46:50.900 --> 00:46:53.980
Some say they were the true office BFFs.

1237
00:46:54.300 --> 00:46:57.780
One of them said that they were each other's work spouse.

1238
00:46:57.980 --> 00:46:59.420
And that really cracked me up.

1239
00:46:59.540 --> 00:47:00.780
I think that's true.

1240
00:47:01.240 --> 00:47:04.020
I found two examples that I loved.

1241
00:47:04.180 --> 00:47:09.780
There are many, but I want to share two of Phyllis and Stanley being each other's work spouse.

1242
00:47:09.780 --> 00:47:13.220
My absolute favorite is a very small moment.

1243
00:47:13.520 --> 00:47:15.500
It's from the episode Blood Drive.

1244
00:47:15.720 --> 00:47:19.260
And they're trying to get free cookies from the Bloodmobile.

1245
00:47:19.500 --> 00:47:20.540
I remember that.

1246
00:47:20.780 --> 00:47:25.520
Stanley goes in first and Phyllis is lurking outside the Bloodmobile like waiting.

1247
00:47:25.820 --> 00:47:26.680
Let's hear it.

1248
00:47:27.220 --> 00:47:29.000
Pardon me, I have a chocolate chip cookie.

1249
00:47:29.120 --> 00:47:31.320
I gave blood earlier and I'm still feeling woozy.

1250
00:47:31.540 --> 00:47:31.920
Of course.

1251
00:47:33.220 --> 00:47:33.980
That's weird.

1252
00:47:34.380 --> 00:47:37.380
You got a cotton ball and tape and we've been using band-aids.

1253
00:47:37.860 --> 00:47:39.400
Oh, I feel so woozy.

1254
00:47:39.400 --> 00:47:42.180
You got just mand-aids.

1255
00:47:46.030 --> 00:47:48.610
So they both put a cotton ball and tape.

1256
00:47:48.750 --> 00:47:53.650
And then when they went in, they found out that that particular Bloodmobile doesn't do it like that.

1257
00:47:54.170 --> 00:47:55.090
It's very funny.

1258
00:47:55.270 --> 00:47:56.010
And it's so funny.

1259
00:47:56.310 --> 00:47:57.470
Phyllis is like, damn it.

1260
00:47:57.770 --> 00:47:59.670
Anyway, it just cracked me up.

1261
00:47:59.750 --> 00:48:00.910
I love the two of them.

1262
00:48:01.030 --> 00:48:05.710
But there is one fan theory that we got a ton of mail about.

1263
00:48:05.950 --> 00:48:07.450
We're going to get to the bottom of it today.

1264
00:48:07.450 --> 00:48:15.370
Several of you wrote in, like Rocco from Canada and many others, saying, did Stanley and Phyllis ever hook up?

1265
00:48:15.590 --> 00:48:21.790
Is Stanley the person Phyllis is talking about when she said she hooked up with someone in the office?

1266
00:48:21.790 --> 00:48:30.690
Angela, I know you're very excited about this because I got a very excited message from you yesterday saying you have an answer.

1267
00:48:30.890 --> 00:48:31.650
I do.

1268
00:48:31.930 --> 00:48:36.110
This was like your mom detective moment about what does Stanley have on his pretzel?

1269
00:48:36.110 --> 00:48:38.410
Yes, that was my obsessive moment this week.

1270
00:48:39.070 --> 00:48:43.670
Well, first of all, there's an article on Looper based off a fan theory.

1271
00:48:43.910 --> 00:48:45.290
The fan theory was on Reddit.

1272
00:48:45.650 --> 00:48:54.690
The user was JoeyH595, who started a thread that suggested the two could have had a sexual relationship before the series was filmed.

1273
00:48:54.910 --> 00:48:58.390
So this would have been a hookup that even predates the pilot.

1274
00:48:58.630 --> 00:49:01.870
They didn't hook up during any part of the show we're watching.

1275
00:49:01.990 --> 00:49:04.350
Yes, according to this fan theory.

1276
00:49:04.470 --> 00:49:04.690
Yes.

1277
00:49:04.690 --> 00:49:08.890
One piece of evidence to support this is in season two's Sexual Harassment.

1278
00:49:09.310 --> 00:49:15.270
Toby reminds the staff that they must disclose any romantic relationships people have with co-workers.

1279
00:49:15.750 --> 00:49:20.510
And then Phyllis promptly says, does that include a one-night stand?

1280
00:49:21.470 --> 00:49:24.690
Suggesting that she had a tryst with someone working close by.

1281
00:49:24.930 --> 00:49:29.590
The show never reveals who it could be, but a lot of people think it might be Stanley.

1282
00:49:29.870 --> 00:49:33.970
Because one, they say, well, they both have a history of adultery.

1283
00:49:33.970 --> 00:49:37.450
Stanley famously cheats on his wife several times.

1284
00:49:37.750 --> 00:49:47.490
And then some people pointed out that in the episode, The Chump, Michael says, why is it okay for Phyllis to cheat on her diet?

1285
00:49:47.790 --> 00:49:49.970
And he makes this pause and he pivots.

1286
00:49:50.130 --> 00:49:57.450
And they think that abrupt pivot means that Michael knew that Phyllis cheated on Bob Vance, but then had to pivot to cover it.

1287
00:49:57.450 --> 00:49:59.410
I don't think Phyllis cheated on Bob Vance.

1288
00:49:59.430 --> 00:50:03.110
I absolutely don't think Phyllis cheated on Bob Vance at all.

1289
00:50:03.990 --> 00:50:06.430
So this leads me to my mom detective moment.

1290
00:50:06.430 --> 00:50:17.530
Because not only is this fan theory, but Leslie shared that one of his favorite scenes that he did with Phyllis ever on the whole show was unfortunately deleted.

1291
00:50:17.570 --> 00:50:22.150
And he said it's where Stanley and Phyllis are having cocktails at their desk.

1292
00:50:22.150 --> 00:50:25.190
Yes, Angela, and I remember you said, oh, I want to find that.

1293
00:50:25.350 --> 00:50:28.850
I'd love to play Leslie's favorite scene with Phyllis.

1294
00:50:28.970 --> 00:50:30.250
And so you went down this road.

1295
00:50:30.250 --> 00:50:31.290
You're looking for it.

1296
00:50:31.370 --> 00:50:32.510
What episode was that?

1297
00:50:32.830 --> 00:50:40.950
Yeah, because I'm like, if they're drinking after hours together, does that support this theory that they have a relationship?

1298
00:50:42.110 --> 00:50:44.090
Well, I couldn't find it anywhere.

1299
00:50:44.630 --> 00:50:46.930
I could not find this deleted scene.

1300
00:50:46.950 --> 00:50:48.450
So I reached out to Dave Rogers.

1301
00:50:48.650 --> 00:50:53.970
He immediately, of course, was like, Angela, that was a tag written for Doomsday.

1302
00:50:54.310 --> 00:50:54.870
It's not.

1303
00:50:54.870 --> 00:50:55.650
I can't believe that.

1304
00:50:55.770 --> 00:50:57.490
I can't believe he was like, oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

1305
00:50:57.850 --> 00:50:59.990
Deleted Stanley Phyllis having cocktails at their desk.

1306
00:51:00.190 --> 00:51:00.730
Doomsday tag.

1307
00:51:00.910 --> 00:51:02.130
Yeah, Doomsday tag.

1308
00:51:02.330 --> 00:51:04.430
He said it's not in deleted scenes.

1309
00:51:04.430 --> 00:51:06.230
It's probably in the shooting draft.

1310
00:51:06.430 --> 00:51:08.230
So I go to the shooting draft.

1311
00:51:08.390 --> 00:51:09.110
It's not there.

1312
00:51:09.350 --> 00:51:11.110
I go to the candy bag alts.

1313
00:51:11.270 --> 00:51:11.990
It's not there.

1314
00:51:13.050 --> 00:51:16.890
Finally, I go to an early table draft that we had.

1315
00:51:17.130 --> 00:51:18.330
And there it is.

1316
00:51:18.530 --> 00:51:19.630
There is the tag.

1317
00:51:19.810 --> 00:51:21.750
And I guess they actually shot it.

1318
00:51:22.410 --> 00:51:22.710
Wow.

1319
00:51:23.050 --> 00:51:25.270
And here is what happens in the tag.

1320
00:51:25.390 --> 00:51:25.850
Are you ready?

1321
