And then Stanley goes to pour Phyllis a drink and it overflows.

1339
00:52:04.150 --> 00:52:06.930
He says, whoops-a-daisy, Stanley's drunk.

1340
00:52:07.250 --> 00:52:11.370
And he looks at the spill and says, have you ever seen anything so sad?

1341
00:52:11.490 --> 00:52:12.290
And they laugh.

1342
00:52:12.290 --> 00:52:15.750
And then Phyllis dabs a little bit of brandy behind her ear.

1343
00:52:16.670 --> 00:52:17.730
Where's this going?

1344
00:52:17.990 --> 00:52:20.230
She says, this drives Bob crazy.

1345
00:52:20.950 --> 00:52:24.650
Then she starts wincing and goes, ow, ow, ow, my eczema.

1346
00:52:24.990 --> 00:52:25.210
Ow.

1347
00:52:25.210 --> 00:52:26.950
He says, okay, it's better.

1348
00:52:27.670 --> 00:52:28.810
Stanley goes, you okay?

1349
00:52:29.110 --> 00:52:31.350
And Phyllis says, yes, thank you for asking.

1350
00:52:32.090 --> 00:52:33.670
Stanley says, you are welcome.

1351
00:52:33.970 --> 00:52:35.810
I'm on the edge of my seat right now.

1352
00:52:35.990 --> 00:52:38.390
Then there is a long pause.

1353
00:52:38.810 --> 00:52:39.330
What?

1354
00:52:39.530 --> 00:52:43.330
And then here's something they say at the same time.

1355
00:52:44.270 --> 00:52:45.290
Overlapping dialogue.

1356
00:52:45.630 --> 00:52:49.850
Overlapping dialogue after a long pause and drinking brandy.

1357
00:52:50.970 --> 00:52:53.170
Stanley says, how's Bob doing?

1358
00:52:54.010 --> 00:52:56.990
Phyllis says, I've never been with a black man before.

1359
00:52:57.390 --> 00:52:57.930
What?

1360
00:52:58.690 --> 00:52:59.230
What?

1361
00:52:59.810 --> 00:53:00.350
Wow.

1362
00:53:00.910 --> 00:53:03.450
And then there is a long beat.

1363
00:53:03.770 --> 00:53:05.970
And Stanley says, good night.

1364
00:53:07.430 --> 00:53:11.190
And he leaves feeling a little awkward and exits.

1365
00:53:11.510 --> 00:53:12.290
Oh, my gosh.

1366
00:53:12.330 --> 00:53:13.530
There's so much to unpack.

1367
00:53:13.830 --> 00:53:14.830
There is so much to unpack.

1368
00:53:15.430 --> 00:53:19.670
Okay, so first of all, it answers the question, they have not hooked up before.

1369
00:53:19.830 --> 00:53:20.790
They've never hooked up.

1370
00:53:20.790 --> 00:53:25.650
But I feel like it sort of teases that in this moment, Phyllis might have.

1371
00:53:25.750 --> 00:53:26.890
Might have been up for it.

1372
00:53:26.950 --> 00:53:27.330
Yes.

1373
00:53:27.530 --> 00:53:30.910
Is this her, I knew what I was doing, Pam moment?

1374
00:53:31.070 --> 00:53:32.650
I think maybe so.

1375
00:53:32.870 --> 00:53:37.330
And, you know, so many fan theories point to these moments where there was tenderness between them,

1376
00:53:37.450 --> 00:53:39.250
even though they got on each other's nerves.

1377
00:53:39.430 --> 00:53:39.650
Yes.

1378
00:53:39.890 --> 00:53:43.830
You know, I mean, Stanley whittled that whole thing for her.

1379
00:53:44.070 --> 00:53:44.390
Phyllis.

1380
00:53:44.550 --> 00:53:44.830
Yeah.

1381
00:53:45.010 --> 00:53:45.850
As a chicken.

1382
00:53:46.090 --> 00:53:46.330
Yes.

1383
00:53:46.330 --> 00:53:46.790
Or whatever.

1384
00:53:47.030 --> 00:53:49.250
As a bird person in the finale.

1385
00:53:49.550 --> 00:53:51.190
I mean, he clearly cares for her.

1386
00:53:51.270 --> 00:53:51.430
Yeah.

1387
00:53:52.170 --> 00:53:56.470
But, yeah, I'm telling you, the long pause is where everything happens.

1388
00:53:57.310 --> 00:53:58.590
Oh, my gosh.

1389
00:53:58.730 --> 00:53:59.670
Put that on a mug.

1390
00:54:00.770 --> 00:54:03.130
So there was my mom detective moment.

1391
00:54:03.390 --> 00:54:04.230
I loved it.

1392
00:54:04.430 --> 00:54:06.630
Thank you, Dave, for pointing me in the right direction.

1393
00:54:06.630 --> 00:54:12.010
But, yeah, I mean, a little bit of brandy, dot, dot, dot.

1394
00:54:12.630 --> 00:54:13.310
Dot, dot.

1395
00:54:13.610 --> 00:54:14.650
But nothing happened.

1396
00:54:14.970 --> 00:54:19.190
And I think that settles it that they had never hooked up.

1397
00:54:19.570 --> 00:54:23.090
Well, in real life, Leslie and Phyllis were very good friends.

1398
00:54:23.290 --> 00:54:24.650
They are still good friends.

1399
00:54:24.790 --> 00:54:32.390
In fact, Leslie said his favorite person to do scenes with is Phyllis because she's an amazing actress and because they are friends in real life.

1400
00:54:32.390 --> 00:54:37.750
And we reached out to Phyllis to ask her about working with Leslie, and she said this.

1401
00:54:38.430 --> 00:54:46.230
Leslie is a real stand-up guy with character and principles and a sense of humor that just adds charm and wit when being with him.

1402
00:54:46.890 --> 00:54:50.170
She confirmed that they did a lot of online shopping together.

1403
00:54:50.310 --> 00:54:56.570
And she said they would also run to Walmart and do errands together if there was ever a long break in filming.

1404
00:54:56.930 --> 00:54:58.050
Could you imagine?

1405
00:54:58.430 --> 00:54:59.250
I know.

1406
00:54:59.490 --> 00:54:59.950
I know.

1407
00:54:59.950 --> 00:55:04.910
Like if they weren't in a couple of scenes in the afternoon, they'd just go hop over to Walmart together.

1408
00:55:05.110 --> 00:55:05.910
It's so adorable.

1409
00:55:06.490 --> 00:55:09.930
And they also would show up for each other at their premieres and things.

1410
00:55:10.150 --> 00:55:15.850
I mean, I saw a picture that Leslie went with Phyllis for her, the OA, the show on Netflix, her premiere.

1411
00:55:16.090 --> 00:55:16.310
Yeah.

1412
00:55:16.390 --> 00:55:17.850
He did the red carpet with her.

1413
00:55:18.430 --> 00:55:21.230
But we all used to get paired up to do press on the show.

1414
00:55:21.450 --> 00:55:23.530
You know, I would get paired up with Brian or Rain.

1415
00:55:23.690 --> 00:55:25.610
You would get paired up with John quite a bit.

1416
00:55:25.710 --> 00:55:26.030
Usually.

1417
00:55:26.270 --> 00:55:28.830
And Phyllis and Leslie were always paired up together.

1418
00:55:28.830 --> 00:55:34.950
Rather, I found an interview of the two of them on the red carpet for the BAFTA tea years ago.

1419
00:55:34.950 --> 00:55:39.470
So they were very excited about things that were coming up for their characters on the show.

1420
00:55:39.570 --> 00:55:41.450
And I watched the whole interview.

1421
00:55:41.450 --> 00:55:45.890
It just warmed my heart because you could just, I don't know, you could hear their love for the show.

1422
00:55:46.030 --> 00:55:48.250
You could hear their familiarity and friendship.

1423
00:55:48.510 --> 00:55:49.930
And I thought I'd share it.

1424
00:55:50.550 --> 00:55:50.990
Hello, sir.

1425
00:55:51.050 --> 00:55:51.570
How are you doing?

1426
00:55:52.510 --> 00:55:53.650
Huge office freak.

1427
00:55:53.970 --> 00:55:54.070
All right.

1428
00:55:54.170 --> 00:55:54.390
Yes.

1429
00:55:54.550 --> 00:55:55.470
It's one of my favorite shows.

1430
00:55:55.470 --> 00:55:57.030
Okay, what can we expect this year?

1431
00:55:57.310 --> 00:55:57.990
Well, we know.

1432
00:55:58.190 --> 00:55:59.250
All the spoilers.

1433
00:56:00.070 --> 00:56:03.010
Well, you already saw Thursday night what happened.

1434
00:56:03.210 --> 00:56:04.230
I have issues.

1435
00:56:05.210 --> 00:56:05.550
I know.

1436
00:56:05.690 --> 00:56:06.370
He's showing up.

1437
00:56:06.450 --> 00:56:11.990
I'm cheating and tearing up cars and just, you know, I'm having a midlife man crisis.

1438
00:56:11.990 --> 00:56:12.670
I don't know.

1439
00:56:12.930 --> 00:56:14.170
Are you happy with that storyline?

1440
00:56:14.850 --> 00:56:17.990
I am because it was so much fun to do.

1441
00:56:18.610 --> 00:56:21.290
And it was unexpected and unpredictable.

1442
00:56:21.590 --> 00:56:22.910
And it surprised me.

1443
00:56:23.010 --> 00:56:24.350
It surprised the other cast members.

1444
00:56:24.410 --> 00:56:25.710
And it was fun to do.

1445
00:56:25.810 --> 00:56:27.270
And it's always nice because he keeps it fresh.

1446
00:56:27.410 --> 00:56:27.690
Absolutely.

1447
00:56:28.230 --> 00:56:28.590
He keeps it fresh, yeah.

1448
00:56:28.910 --> 00:56:30.510
You know, get to stretch your acting chops.

1449
00:56:30.910 --> 00:56:34.090
You guys actually stick to the script more than we assume you do, right?

1450
00:56:35.110 --> 00:56:37.110
Well, usually we lay the script out.

1451
00:56:37.210 --> 00:56:39.370
It depends on the director and his style of directing.

1452
00:56:39.370 --> 00:56:42.270
But they would like for us to lay it down as written.

1453
00:56:42.290 --> 00:56:44.310
And then they say, okay, play with it.

1454
00:56:44.410 --> 00:56:45.390
And then we're allowed to.

1455
00:56:45.390 --> 00:56:49.690
And then it goes places you never dreamed of.

1456
00:56:49.710 --> 00:56:51.030
Don't you see any deleted scenes?

1457
00:56:52.710 --> 00:56:54.130
Oh, I loved that.

1458
00:56:54.410 --> 00:56:57.810
You got to share that, Angela, so that people can watch the whole thing.

1459
00:56:58.030 --> 00:56:59.510
That was just a little snippet.

1460
00:56:59.650 --> 00:57:00.130
I will.

1461
00:57:00.230 --> 00:57:03.010
I think I just love that you hear Leslie's laugh.

1462
00:57:03.210 --> 00:57:06.990
And, you know, he's just full of joy and so not like his Stanley character.

1463
00:57:06.990 --> 00:57:08.450
And I thought it was nice to hear that.

